.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH rev-stealth-config-history 1  "rev-stealth-config-history " 
.SH NAME
rev\-stealth\-config\-history \- P6.4: List the `.bak.<epoch>` backups for the target config file in newest→oldest order (sorted by mtime, tie\-broken by filename desc to match the epoch\-ms suffix)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrev\-stealth config history\fR [\fB\-\-target\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
List the .bak.<epoch> backups for the target config file in newest→oldest order. Sorted by mtime, ties broken by filename desc (matching the epoch\-ms suffix).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-target\fR \fI<TARGET>\fR [default: policy]
Which file\*(Aqs backups to list. Defaults to `policy`
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
policy
.IP \(bu 2
authorized
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH EXTRA
EXAMPLES:
  $ rev\-stealth config history
  $ rev\-stealth config history \-\-target authorized

EXIT CODES:
  0  Ok               Listing emitted.
  1  UserError        Unknown target.
  3  PermanentError   directory IO failure.

ENV:
  REV_SCRAPING_POLICY      Override the policy.toml path.
  REV_SCRAPING_AUTHORIZED  Override the authorized.toml path.
